Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Heel Four Arrives Before the Sub
- Story & Context: The debut runs at 120 BPM. Ivana begins with a four-note lijerica figure over an open drone while her heel stamps steady quarter notes. Ellis programs the simplest steppers kick possible, but the sub does not enter with the kick. Instead, each low note arrives a short moment after every fourth heel-stamp, making the floor impact feel like a physical warning before the electronic weight appears. Petra plays one damped suspended-second chord only when the bow accent and heel accent coincide. Luka replaces every fourth electronic rim with one frame-drum center hit. Maeve waits until the lijerica moves upward, then enters on a low contrabass-clarinet fifth. In the final section the electronic kick is muted for four bars, but Ivana keeps stamping and bowing. When the kick returns, it feels like it has rejoined an acoustic pulse that never stopped.
